{
  "renderer": "NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 Ti. Actual production skinned game GLBs, 1024 px atlas, neutral pose, fixed body and 64 degrees yaw / 14 degrees elevation for coat pairs, 72 / 12 for isolated limbs. Gameplay comparisons and limb crops share camera, scale and light. Coat close crops use the same algorithm on each simplified GLB. On the two frozen sheets their relative camera scale differs by less than 0.006 percent and crop centre by at most 1.93 pixels. The hardware reader samples vertex colour, albedo and mesh normals; it does not sample material roughness or the normal texture in the blind images.",
  "sources": "Original locally generated workshop geometry and colour only. All four microtexture swatches are rasterized from procedural code. No external images, models, scanned materials or practice assets.",
  "hypothesis": "A material that fits the anatomy and layers pigment across regions can improve whole-character appeal and close detail while retaining the original design.",
  "eligibleDesign": "Both six-animal runs are consecutive and unselected. Before always uses the saved ordinary original form. The broad-coverage trials used the suggested family for each animal and preserve the same geometry recipe. GPU simplification may choose different surviving vertices when their colours change. The first two revisions were rejected. Repeated development examples and one blind reader per sheet limit inference.",
