  "isolatedLimbTest": {
    "hypothesis": "Fade the existing dark-tip colour along segment length to remove the cuff while preserving the rest of the animal and its original markings.",
    "operation": "steerCreature, set.skin={coat:null,limbFade:true}; compare to the same plan with limbFade:false. Dark limb ends remains a 0–1 amount. New draws with dark socks enable the fade. Older stored recipes retain their authored look.",
    "sampling": "First three eligible in seed windows starting 9100 and 9350, then first four eligible from 9390. Eligibility fixed at dark-tip amount > .45 and at least one leg. A single reviewer per randomly mixed sheet. Each side shows 146 px gameplay and one crop selected by most forward near-side shin.",
    "pilotImage": "creature-limb-colour-pilot.webp",
    "holdoutImage": "creature-limb-colour-held.webp",
    "metric": "For each upper/forearm and thigh/shin pair take vertex pigment multiplied by atlas albedo in linear light, then convert to 8-bit sRGB. Sample each segment 7%–30% of its length away from the joint on its outward surface (normal X times side > .23), minimum four vertices per sample. Measure RMS difference across RGB channels between the two median colours. Compare only joints eligible in both GLBs. Co-located welded vertices had zero or too few pairs, so they alone cannot measure the cuff.",
